" Slate's starting Vim config
"
" Slate made this because you had no vimrc of your own (Settings → Appearance → App
" theming). It's yours now: change anything. Switching Vim off in App theming deletes
" this file if you haven't changed it, or just the colorscheme line if you have.

" Vim's usual defaults (having any vimrc of your own turns them off, so load them here)
source $VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim

" Slate's colours (colors/slate-desktop.vim), rewritten whenever Slate's theme changes
colorscheme slate-desktop
